    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise atan using three range intervals and a rational approximation.\n2: \n3: Synthetic FP32 Triton adaptation of Cephes atan.c, Release 2.8 (June 2000).\n4: The original Cephes source credits Stephen L. Moshier, copyright 1984,\n5: 1995 and 2000. This is not a claim of an upstream historical defect.\n6: Source: https://netlib.org/cephes/cmath.tgz (atan.c).\n7: \"\"\"\n8: import torch\n9: import triton\n10: import triton.language as tl\n11: \n12: \n13: @triton.jit\n14: def _atan_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n15:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n16:     active = index < N\n17:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n18:     magnitude = tl.abs(x)\n19:     upper = magnitude > 2.414213562373095\n20:     middle = magnitude > 0.66\n21:     reciprocal = -tl.div_rn(1.0, tl.maximum(magnitude, 1.0))\n22:     centered = tl.div_rn(magnitude - 1.0, magnitude + 1.0)\n23:     reduced = tl.where(upper, reciprocal, tl.where(middle, centered, magnitude))\n24:     angle = tl.where(upper, 1.5707963267948966,\n25:                      tl.where(middle, 0.7853981633974483, 0.0))\n26:     square = reduced * reduced\n27:     numerator = -0.8751\n28:     numerator = numerator * square + -16.16\n29:     numerator = numerator * square + -75.01\n30:     numerator = numerator * square + -122.9\n31:     numerator = numerator * square + -64.85\n32:     denominator = square + 24.86\n33:     denominator = denominator * square + 165.0\n34:     denominator = denominator * square + 432.9\n35:     denominator = denominator * square + 485.4\n36:     denominator = denominator * square + 194.6\n37:     correction = tl.div_rn(square * numerator, denominator)\n38:     local_angle = reduced * correction + reduced\n39:     value = angle + local_angle\n40:     value = tl.where(x < 0.0, -value, value)\n41:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n42: \n43: \n44: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n45:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n46:     def require(condition, message):\n47:         if not condition:\n48:             raise ValueError(message)\n49: \n50:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n51:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n52:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n53:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n54:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n55:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n56:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n57:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n58:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n59:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n60:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n61:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n62:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n63:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n64: \n65: \n66: def run(x):\n67:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor approximating atan of each stored input value.\"\"\"\n68:     validate_inputs(x)\n69:     n = x.numel()\n70:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n71:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n72:         _atan_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n73:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n74:     return output\n75: \n76: \n77: def reference(x):\n78:     \"\"\"Evaluate mathematical atan independently using the FP64 library function.\"\"\"\n79:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n80:     return torch.atan(x.to(torch.float64))\n81: \n82: \n83: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n84:     \"\"\"Convenience example generator, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n85:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n86:     x = (2.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n87:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute atan elementwise on stored FP16 values, returning FP32 output.\nThe mathematical target is target[i] = atan(x[i]), in radians.\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided, contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False, is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode, without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x. Every output element must satisfy:\n\n  abs(actual[i] - atan(x[i])) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent. The target is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value. No particular range reduction, rational approximation or intermediate rounding is part of the mathematical target. Algebraic rewrites and approximations are permitted if they satisfy this fixed absolute tolerance throughout the entire legal domain. Correctness is one verdict for the implementation, not a verdict per input, input distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference() uses the independent FP64 library atan and returns FP64; it accepts CPU inputs. make_inputs() supplies examples only. This is a synthetic FP32 Triton adaptation of the range-reduced rational form in Cephes atan, not a reproduction of an upstream historical defect. The original double-precision implementation's accuracy claim does not establish this adaptation's accuracy.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch 2.8.0, Triton 3.4.0.\n",
